[Music]  hulu's newest marvel show is a different  breed than what comic fans have been  watching on disney plus  putting the focus on a very unlikely  leading man modoc the marvel comics  references come as fast as the jokes in  modoc and it's hard to catch them all  here's a look at all the easter eggs you  may have missed  we see aim scientist supreme monica  rappuccini's daughter carmilla black in  a couple of scenes throughout the season  mostly interacting with modoc's son  lou anyone unfamiliar with the character  would be forgiven for not paying the  design of her outfit much attention as  it goes with her goth attire but her  white scorpion is a hint to her future  comics persona  in the comics monica messed with her  daughter's genetic makeup which becomes  apparent to the teenager when her toxin  powers manifest and cause carmilla to  kill her boyfriend  at their prom she takes up the name  scorpion and looks to avenge the people  she believed to be her parents  working for both sides and even being  sent to track down her own mother at one  point it's an interesting relationship  to say the least  save me joy division early in the season  modoc sets out to find his time machine  but we learned that it was actually  monica who built it the device or at  least the celestial chrono crystal that  powers it  becomes a huge part of the show's plot  at some point the device was apparently  confiscated by shield which means modok  must break onto a helicarrier to  retrieve the time machine in an effort  to save his relationship  one not so clever disguise later and  modoc is looking through boxes in a  shield storage locker finding all sorts  of nifty things from across the marvel  universe  fans of the x-men movies probably perked  up at the mention of the cerebro but  modok pulling out the ultimate nullifier  is a great little easter egg for die  hard marvel comics fans  it was used by the fantastic four to  convince galactus not to mess with earth  so it's pretty important which is why  modok's casual dismissal of it is so  perfect episode 4 has modoc form a team  for a heist but first they have to  retrieve team member 10 pins exploding  pins which takes the crew to the always  darkest before the pawn  pawn shop it's a great setup for  spotting familiar items from the marvel  universe like ant-man's helmet the real  treat in this shop however is all of the  x-men memorabilia the nightcrawler  plushie behind the counter is cute and  easy enough to spot but keynite viewers  will also notice that the mask on the  counter belongs to a hellfire club  soldier  magic soul sword mounted on the wall and  dazzler's silver skates from her  performing days  fenfang fume is a bit of a silly  character in the eyes of most fans but  he's also one that's been around for  quite a long time  a product of the 1960s he debuted in  strange tales number 89.  this shape-shifting alien's most widely  known form resembles that of a chinese  dragon  helping him on a mission to conquer  earth in modoc austin takes modak to a  restaurant called  finfeng farm to table where he cooks the  food with his fire breath  this may seem like a simple joke using  his name and dragon like abilities but  it's also a reference to a comic story  in 2005's  fenfang 4 where fume reforms and becomes  a chef  working inside the fantastic four's  baxter building in another episode modok  has a dream about flying on foom and  cheering  looking down at his utopian city this is  a reference to 1984's the never-ending  story and it's a moment that will stir  some major nostalgia for people who grew  up with it  at least until modoc's dream ends  abruptly and we see the state his life  is in  even modoc loves to socialize and drink  with his fellow villainous scum but the  big names aren't down for partying with  him this brings him to the bar with no  name  a joint that has become rather infamous  in the comics not just because of its  clientele but for the violence that  tends to occur there  usually this particular haven acts as a  safe spot but that doesn't always work  out for the version viewers are shown in  modoc we get quite the array of b-list  villain guest stars armadillo melter  angar the screamer pound cakes and  10-pin all play into the plot while  whirlwind makes an appearance and orb  acts as the bartender it's an amusing  introduction to a list of usually  forgettable characters whose hijinks  eventually lead the audience to also see  mandrill and much more of him than most  probably wanted to  the thing is a founding member of the  fantastic four and someone who has  helped save the world his fair share of  times but many out there feel old ben  grimm  has never truly received the respect he  deserves modok only gives him the  smallest of nods with his fist appearing  as part of a commercial  advertising alcohol with wolverine's  distinctive claw but if you look closely  the thing also gets one other brief nod  when modok and his group are riding the  subway some graffiti plastered above  them reads yancy street gang rules  this is a reference to a local group  from ben's old neighborhood who are not  necessarily criminals but more  mischief makers and serial harassers who  have it out for the thing  david cannon is a mutant super villain  better known as whirlwind he pops up a  couple of times in modoc wearing all  green armor with saw blades but he  doesn't have much to do with the overall  narrative  there is however a fun reference to the  character's comics origin  just before melissa modoc's daughter  wrenches whirlwind's arm and slams his  face onto the bar he's trying to  congratulate her on a great triple axel  she pulled off  hey congrats on that triple axel i get a  real pleasure out of watching you skank  formerly known as the human top  whirlwind was also a figure skater at  one point  back when his criminal exploits were  just beginning to blossom  modoc is full of guest stars fun cameos  and brief sightings that aren't  necessarily hard to spot but not all of  these are exactly well-known characters  even for fans of the comics  they're saying you're not a top-tier  super villain when wonder man shows up  to handle tattered demelian he's at  least  identified by name but that isn't true  for a lot of the others  hip-hop a literal cyborg kangaroo is  seen on a billboard but at least his  name is visible if anyone wants to look  him up and see if he's a real character  that time has forgotten  which he is a few more cameos come in a  scene when modoc is going through a list  of various portal dimensions  showing the scrolls one of the shiar  that looks a lot like lalondra  a watcher and the brood who makes an  appearance later in the episode but what  about mr waffles the bunny a character  from the 40s better known as super  rabbit  that's definitely a weird and well  hidden reference there's also a brief  scene with a demonic talk show host  named master pandemonium who  inexplicably has two baby demons for  hands hardcore fans will know that those  weird hands are definitely from the  comics and it's creepy to see them no  matter what  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  marvel comics movies and tv shows are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

